+- **Label forms.** The label takes exactly one of four forms, tested in this
+  order; the first whose condition holds applies.
+  - **Not read**, when the tag set was not captured, because its input is not
+    admitted or reading it failed. Polaris names the revision by its first
+    twelve hexadecimal digits beside the statement that release tags were not
+    read, the reason `source-uncaptured-or-unreachable` and its route. It
+    never states that the revision is untagged.
+  - **Tagged**, when a captured tag reaches the revision at distance zero.
+    The label is the project's name followed by that tag's name.
+  - **Described**, when some captured tag reaches the revision. The label is
+    the project's name, the name of the reaching tag with the least distance,
+    and that distance stated as a count of later commits.
+  - **Untagged**, otherwise. The label is the project's name and the
+    revision's first twelve hexadecimal digits, beside the statement that no
+    release tag reaches this revision.
+  - Where tags tie for the least distance, the label names the first of them
+    in codepoint order of tag name, and every tied name is carried in the
+    machine answer and expandable on the surface.
